OL,3,AEconomic adviser O'Neill rules out
OL,4,Agovernment job but backs PM's
OL,5,Adevolution plans
OL,6,
OL,7,FEconomist Lord Jim O'Neill, who has
OL,8,Fbeen advising the prime minister, has
OL,9,Fsaid he will not be taking a job in
OL,10,FAndy Burnham's government.
OL,12,FAs first reported by the Financial
OL,13,FTimes, Lord O'Neill, a crossbench peer
OL,14,Fwho was once a treasury minister under
OL,15,Fthe Conservatives, said he did not want
OL,16,Fthe constraints involved in taking on a
OL,17,Fformal role.
OL,19,FThe former chief economist at Goldman
OL,20,FSachs had been tipped to become
OL,21,FBurnham's chief economic adviser.
OL,23,APub: 22-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
